{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"0c79225bf667efba972fac43d4f950efb75d60beaf20297656a11c3d9cf66395","slug":"jupyter-parameterized-kernel-specs","location":"/87-jupyter-parameterized-kernel-spec/jupyter-parameterized-kernel-specs.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Jupyter Parameterized Kernel Specs","authors":[{"id":"Carlos Herrero, Anastasiia Sliusar","name":"Carlos Herrero, Anastasiia Sliusar"}],"date":"2026-02-05","content_includes_title":false,"github":"https://github.com/jupyter/enhancement-proposals","numbering":{"title":{"offset":1}},"source_url":"https://github.com/jupyter/enhancement-proposals/blob/main/87-jupyter-parameterized-kernel-spec/jupyter-parameterized-kernel-specs.md","edit_url":"https://github.com/jupyter/enhancement-proposals/edit/main/87-jupyter-parameterized-kernel-spec/jupyter-parameterized-kernel-specs.md","thumbnail":"/enhancement-proposals/build/launcher-0252edc7b61180a91c2fe6f1724451c8.png","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"jupyter-parameterized-kernel-specs.md","url":"/enhancement-proposals/build/jupyter-parameterize-c1aec5a1f6d7fb0fafd65b80e5c27f0f.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Problem","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"key":"rosHIq3dk1"}],"identifier":"problem","label":"Problem","html_id":"problem","implicit":true,"key":"r00UcVrgM0"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"When creating a new kernel, we need to define a different “specs” file for each possible parameter combination used by the executable. For example, the xeus-cling kernel supports three different versions of the ","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"uRKMpA0Dj6"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"C++","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"piPor04PAu"},{"type":"text","value":" language, ","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"FIBNkQyUDQ"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"C++11","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"Q7p6njmNYf"},{"type":"text","value":", ","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"jdRskbcBMz"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"C++14","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"KgrlYcT6rH"},{"type":"text","value":", and ","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"lHAKxBSYPg"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"C++17","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"HJfZBIdL5C"},{"type":"text","value":", which is specified by the ","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"uV40VQ3toe"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--std","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"d90DUwlCov"},{"type":"text","value":" command-line option.","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"TuBJu5YMzG"}],"key":"jVfxxNmX1l"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"When installing xeus-cling, we install three almost identical kernel specs. The only difference is the last parameter of the execution command ","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"key":"N4jyYXzW2v"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--std=c++X","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"key":"tDha1yRq3n"},{"type":"text","value":".","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"key":"UV4gLbwqHr"}],"key":"oiAq05p4xs"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":21,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"When more than one parameter is available, the number of possible combinations grows in a combinatorics fashion.","position":{"start":{"line":21,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"key":"TrZUlVjNac"}],"key":"Xk4PTpvz2H"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":23,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Besides, some kernels would benefit from being configurable when launching them. For example, the connection information to the database could be specified through kernel parameters rather than kernel magics.","position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":23,"column":1}},"key":"pPSbQ4B4wx"}],"key":"YvGFBb6OkJ"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sometimes when installing multiple kernels, the JupyterLab launcher panel is crowded with too many options to create a notebook or console with a specific kernel. The kernels that users see in the launcher are just multiple kernel specs for one kernel. We could avoid having that many kernels displayed, adding parameters to the kernel specs, showing only one option per kernel, and offering a modal dialog with the different options the user can choose from when selecting a specific kernel.","position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"key":"nMfKSQ8xr9"}],"key":"BxopMMhQb7"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Proposed Enhancement","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"key":"oOZJAu6FVh"}],"identifier":"proposed-enhancement","label":"Proposed Enhancement","html_id":"proposed-enhancement","implicit":true,"key":"tH6KIaF6P9"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The solution we are proposing consists of adding parameters to the kernel specs file in the form of a JSON Schema that would be added to the specs metadata. These parameters are then used to populate the ","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"key":"TuIq4uOd6f"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"argv","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"key":"IZvaTdGmpY"},{"type":"text","value":" list and ","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"key":"t5y0xmXSiw"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"env","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"key":"nRuOhR7Pl4"},{"type":"text","value":" dict (respectively the command-line arguments and environment variables).","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"key":"hKPgXtbqmB"}],"key":"EtBlUYoRnb"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Upon starting a new kernel instance, a front-end form generated from the JSON schema is prompted to the user to fill the parameter values. Many tools are available to generate such forms, such as react-jsonschema-form.","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"XUzLPvy6u9"}],"key":"n1OyMysJSV"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"These kernel parameters will be not saved into the notebook due to security reason. The app will have ","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"eGyXzoIqng"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"allowed_insecure_kernelspec_params","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"QjYi3ftt6b"},{"type":"text","value":" flag which will detect whether we have to accept all kernel spec files as safe or not.","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},